      <size maxheight='1020' maxwidth='1000' minheight='1020' minwidth='1000' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='80785' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='18431'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15' underline='true'>CPP</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>1. Uplift: Comparing difference in metric (GFV, orders, customers etc.) during the same time period before CPP and when CPP was running</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12' italic='true'>- E.g. If CPP is running for 15 days, we compare difference in metrics (GFV, orders, customers) 15 days ago vs during the CPP period of 15 days</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>2. Shop Loads: Number of times vendor was loaded on front end</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>3. ROI: GFV uplift / Amount spent on CPP</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>4. ROI (Adjusted): GFV uplift / Amount spent on CPP - but this takes into account inflation or deflation in country&apos;s GFV </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12' italic='true'>- e.g. If  GFV uplift during CPP period was 20% but overall country&apos;s GFV increased by 10%, we will take the country&apos;s uplift of 10% into account</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15' underline='true'>Pandabox</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>1. Pandabox winback customer: If a customer has previously purchased from the vendor and purchases again from vendor with pandabox, it is considered as a winback customer.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>2. Pandabox reorder: If customer first buys from pandabox and then orders again from the same vendor, it is considered a pandabox reorder.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>3. CAC: Cost of acquisition per customer (Cost of pandabox / number of pandabox customers)</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>4. Organic uplift: Uplift in orders, GFV, customers when pandabox is </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'>NOT</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'> used (i.e. is_joker_used is FALSE) </run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15' underline='true'>AND</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='15'> when order is not a pandabox reorder.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='11044' id='359' type-v2='dashboard-object' w='32500' x='800' y='784'>
            <button action='tabdoc:goto-sheet window-id=&quot;{0CAC421F-8C25-4E83-87A3-EB9D7293FA39}&quot;' button-type='text'>
